# Valgrind suppressions for antimony's test suite (used via
# MEMORYCHECK_SUPPRESSIONS_FILE, see CMakeLists.txt / `ctest -T memcheck`).
#
# This starts empty (well, with a couple of extremely common, well-known
# entries below) rather than pre-populated with guesses, since the real
# noise floor -- dynamic loader internals, libSBML/Xerces/expat static
# initializers, the C++ runtime, SWIG/Python interpreter startup if the
# Python bindings get exercised, etc. -- can only be identified accurately
# by actually running `ctest -T memcheck` once and reading Testing/Temporary/
# MemoryChecker.*.log (or the DynamicAnalysis.xml summary) for what's real
# vs. noise.
#
# To add a new suppression: run with --gen-suppressions=yes (or
# --gen-suppressions=all) added to MEMORYCHECK_COMMAND_OPTIONS temporarily,
# copy the block valgrind prints for a confirmed-benign report, and paste it
# below with a comment explaining why it's safe to ignore.

{
   dl_init-ld.so-reachable-not-a-leak
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:_dl_init
   ...
}

{
   libstdc++-iostream-init-once-static
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   ...
   fun:_ZNSt8ios_base4InitC1Ev
   ...
}
